cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use H2STAR, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "H2STAR: an open, uncertainty-aware materials-to-system model for sorbent-based hydrogen storage"
abstract: >-
  H2STAR translates the measurable adsorption properties of carbon sorbents into
  the system-level gravimetric and volumetric performance of a complete onboard
  hydrogen-storage tank, under externally pre-registered calibration and
  held-out validation gates whose outcome - including one disclosed failure and
  the fork rule it triggered - is binding on the claims. It couples real-gas
  hydrogen thermodynamics, a modified Dubinin-Astakhov supercritical isotherm
  fitted to dual-digitized, uncertainty-tagged data under an errors-in-pressure
  measurement model, a component-resolved vessel and system model, profile-
  likelihood identifiability analysis, MCMC uncertainty propagation and Shapley-
  effect attribution. Its central finding is methodological: a single published
  isotherm leaves the isotherm parameters practically non-identifiable while
  constraining system predictions to a few per cent, so requirements should be
  stated in observable quantities - deliverable uptake and packing density -
  rather than as isotherm parameters.
